#: ../../../cute/contracts.md:34
msgid "Disjoint writes across threads."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/contracts.md:36
msgid "Two rules worth remembering"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/contracts.md:38
msgid ""
"**SM100 collective TMA loads.** `Sm100ClusterTmaCopy::copy` needs all 32 "
"lanes of the producer warp with identical arguments; the operation elects a "
"lane internally. An outer elected-lane branch deadlocks once a stage is "
"reused. TMA stores have one issuing thread, so this rule does not apply to "
"them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/contracts.md:43
msgid ""
"**Collector buffers on SM100 and SM107.** Tensor Cores have a small internal "
"scratchpad called a **collector** that can stash an input operand so the "
"next MMA reuses it without reading shared memory again:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/contracts.md:47
msgid ""
"SM100 paired FP16 (`Sm100TiledMma`, automatic per K16 step):\n"
"  first N partition   ──►  fill the A collector\n"
"  second N partition  ──►  last use of the A collector\n"
"\n"
"SM107 MXFP8 (`SM107BlockScaledMmaMXF8F6F4Op`, explicit `BCollector` type "
"marker):\n"
"  top M half    (`CollectorFill`)    ──►  reads B from SMEM and stashes B in "
"the collector\n"
"  bottom M half (`CollectorLastUse`) ──►  reuses B from the collector and "
"frees the slot\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/contracts.md:57
msgid ""
"In `Sm100TiledMma`, the paired operation owns both halves so you cannot "
"leave the A collector dangling. In `SM107BlockScaledMmaMXF8F6F4Op`, you "
"choose `CollectorDiscard`, `CollectorFill`, or `CollectorLastUse` in the "
"type parameters, and you own pairing each `CollectorFill` with a matching "
"`CollectorLastUse` on the same `K = 64` sub-step."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/contracts.md:62
msgid "Grid-constant launch arguments"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/contracts.md:64
msgid ""
"#[grid_constant] desc: &TensorMap<...>\n"
"\n"
"host descriptor  ──►  128-byte launch argument  ──►  device &TensorMap<...>\n"
"                      aligned to 64 bytes            same address for every "
"thread\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/contracts.md:71
msgid ""
"The descriptor needs no device allocation. The full launch contract is under "
"[Kernels and Device Functions](../gpu-programming/kernels-and-device-"
"functions.md)."
msgstr ""
